    <briefdescription>
<para>Fixed-capacity storage, iterated from oldest to newest. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Inserting into a full buffer overwrites its oldest element; inserting at capacity zero does nothing. Raw storage is allocated only on construction or capacity changes. Only live elements are constructed and destroyed; unused capacity is left untouched. Elements themselves may allocate memory.</para>
<para>Copies own their elements independently. Structural modifications invalidate iterators. Access from multiple threads requires external synchronization. </para>
    </detaileddescription>
